Name: Expat XML Parser
Short Name: expat
URL: https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat
Version: R_2_9_0
CPEPrefix: cpe:/a:libexpat_project:libexpat:2.9.0
Date: 2026-10-29
Revision: a76b1174c1ea52abb639a4c69d52b630a8a106a2
Update Mechanism: Manual
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes
License: MIT
License File: src/expat/COPYING

Description:
  This is Expat XML parser - very lightweight C library for parsing XML.
  Expat is distributed under an MIT license detailed in src/expat/COPYING.

  We include it here because libjingle depends on it.

Roll process:
  Expat is rolled to upstream release tags (upstream/R_X_Y_Z). If a roll
  needs more than the DEPS and README.chromium changes, e.g. new upstream
  source files or configure changes, roll by hand:

  cd $CHROMIUM_SRC
  roll-dep --roll-to upstream/R_X_Y_Z src/third_party/expat/src/
  cd $CHROMIUM_SRC/third_party/expat/src/expat
  ./buildconf.sh
  ./configure --without-arc4random --without-arc4random-buf --without-getentropy --without-getrandom --without-sys-getrandom --with-dev-urandom
  cp expat_config.h $CHROMIUM_SRC/third_party/expat/include/expat_config/
  cd $CHROMIUM_SRC/third_party/expat

  Then update the README.chromium and BUILD.gn as needed.
  This can usually by handled by running roll-expat.sh from $CHROMIUM_SRC.

Added files:
  include/expat_config/expat_config.h (a generated config file)
